cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use npready in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "npready: enforcement-readiness analysis for Kubernetes NetworkPolicies"
abstract: >-
  A tool and evaluation framework that measures whether a generated Kubernetes
  NetworkPolicy is safe to enforce: it derives the dependency edges a workload
  declares it needs (from env vars, Ingress, RBAC, DNS, headless peers), reconciles
  them against what the policies admit to surface the "would break on enforce" set,
  scores generators on over-privilege and false-deny, and ships an ATT&CK-mapped,
  declaratively-deployable attack roster to validate what a policy blocks.
type: software
authors:
